      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Parkinson disease can present remarkably as shoulder pains that may long precede the clinical diagnosis. A case is presented in which, during a 2-year period, both lower biceps brachii became exquisitely painful, with both the pain and the \"frozen shoulders\" responding promptly to the initiation of L-dopa therapy."},
